Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The barra kernel tree (kernel/) is a modified Android Generic Kernel Image and
is licensed under GPLv2, matching its upstream. See kernel/COPYING.

Upstream projects barra builds on
---------------------------------

barra patches and rebuilds several upstream projects. Our patches and kernels are
Apache-2.0; the upstream files they apply to keep their own licence.

  llama.cpp              MIT          src/ggml-barra/, src/llama-mali/
                                      TPU attention offload + Mali GPU kernels
  whisper.cpp            MIT          src/whisper-mali/
                                      TPU encoder path + Mali GPU build
  stable-diffusion.cpp   MIT          src/sd-mali/
                                      Mali GEMM and FlashAttention kernels
  sherpa-onnx (k2-fsa)   Apache-2.0   src/pyannote/
                                      replaces the ONNX speaker-embedding
                                      extractor with a TPU implementation
  AOSP / GKI kernel      GPLv2        kernel/
                                      config and patches; full tree included

None of these upstream sources are redistributed here in binary form except where
noted; barra ships patches and build recipes, and builds them on the device or on
the user's machine.

Documentation under docs/ is licensed under CC BY 4.0.

This project does NOT redistribute any Google factory images, proprietary vendor
firmware, or Magisk binaries. Those are fetched from their original sources at
setup time on the user's machine (see barra-setup/), and remain under their
respective licenses and terms.

