Derived model artifacts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

barra ships TPU packages and kits that are DERIVED from third-party models (the
weights, re-quantized and re-laid-out for the Tensor G3 TPU). A derived artifact
carries the licence of the model it came from, not ours. The full chain — which
artifact came from which model, under which licence, with which obligations — is
in docs/models.md, generated from barra-setup/licenses.psd1.

Built with GLM-Edge.
  The TPU attention packages for GLM-Edge-4B-Chat are derived from Zhipu AI's
  GLM-Edge model and are covered by the GLM-Edge License, a copy of which is in
  docs/licenses/GLM-Edge-LICENSE.txt. Commercial use requires registration with
  the model provider; military and unlawful use are prohibited.

Whisper packages are derived from OpenAI's Whisper (MIT). Speaker-diarization
artifacts are derived from wespeaker and 3D-Speaker (Apache-2.0) and from
NVIDIA NeMo TitaNet (CC BY 4.0 — attribution required). The wake-word kit
contains the sherpa-onnx keyword spotter by k2-fsa (Apache-2.0). The speech kit
contains Piper voices (MIT) and a CPython runtime (PSF).

No proprietary vendor firmware or vendor libraries are redistributed. The
Edge-TPU compiler library is generated on the device from the vendor library
that is already installed there; it never leaves the phone.

barra-setup/tools/lpmake.exe is built from AOSP's lpmake (part of the Android Open
Source Project, Apache License 2.0). Google publishes no Windows build, so barra
compiles its own from unmodified upstream sources and bundles the result; the build
recipe is in docs/building-lpmake.md. Copyright (c) The Android Open Source Project.

